<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is immediate from the definition that if $\calC $ is a $\infty $-category, then $M=\Hom ^{\rght }_{\calC }(x,y)$ satisfies the Kan extension condition for every horn inclusion $\Lambda ^ n_ i \subseteq \Delta ^ n$ where $0 < i \leq n$. This implies that $M$ is a Kan complex (Proposition <a href="/tag/9FABF2" data-tag="9FABF2">1.2.5.1</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>